<title>USA: Cooper Cameron Corp Q3 shr rises to $0.72.</title>
<headline>Cooper Cameron Corp Q3 shr rises to $0.72.</headline>
<dateline>HOUSTON 1996-10-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>1996			1995</p>
<p> Shr    profit	    $0.72   profit	 $0.26</p>
<p> Net    profit	   19,300   profit	 6,500</p>
<p> Revs		     378,800		  335,200</p>
<p> Avg shrs		  26,800		   25,600</p>
<p>	  Nine months</p>
<p> Shr    profit	    $1.50     loss	$18.76</p>
<p> Net    profit	   39,800     loss     472,300</p>
<p> Revs		     971,900		  858,300</p>
<p> Avg shrs		  26,500		   25,200</p>
<p>(All data above 000s except per share numbers)</p>
<p>NOTES: 1996 Q3 includes a $1 million or $0.03 per share charge for ongoing cost rationalization efforts in the compression and power equipment segment and certain integration costs for the June 1996 acquisition of Ingram Cactus Co.</p>
<p>1995 Q3 includes a $1.2 million or $0.04 per share after-tax charge for employee severance accruals.</p>
